<title>POLAND: Traders baffled by Wedel 9.9 pct tumble.</title>
<headline>Traders baffled by Wedel 9.9 pct tumble.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish confectioner Wedel SA plunged 9.9 percent to 164.5 zlotys in a 3.5-million-zloty turnover after surging 9.9 percent on Wednesday and left traders puzzled by the stock's rapid swings.</p>
<p>&quot;It's hard to say what caused the fall, one may say it's profit-taking after yesterday's surge, which many thought was a speculative play before the release of September earnings, but now such an explanation doesn't seem to add up,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Wedel earnings report is due on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
